   NO ERROR(S) IN PASS 2

PL/I-80 V1.4 COMPILATION OF: E49H2

   1 a 0000 E49H2:
   2 a 0006   procedure options(main);
   3 a 0006   /* [E2E-49/P4] qualified LEFT, BARE RIGHT, SWAPPED relation:
   4 a 0006      `rec.na > nb' (3/3 written, equal extents).  Twin built from
   5 a 0006      the laws: `> ' swaps, collapse 06 03 / 78 survives the swap
   6 a 0006      (keyed on numbers, [C346]), strict JNC d2.  A PASS-2 refusal
   7 a 0006      here would be a qualification gate INSIDE the relation family
   8 a 0006      only -- invisible to =/^= per [C344] -- a first-class DR
   9 a 0006      boundary, not noise. */
  10 c 0006   dcl
  11 c 0006     1 rec,
  12 c 0006       2 na char(3),
  13 c 0006       2 nb char(3),
  14 c 0006       2 s2 char(2);
  15 c 0006   dcl k fixed bin(15);
  16 c 0006   if rec.na > nb then k = 1;
  17 c 001D   put list('K=', k);
  18 c 003F   stop;
  19 a 0042 end E49H2;

CODE SIZE = 0042
DATA AREA = 000C
FREE SYMS = 3888
END  COMPILATION
